First, choose one connection method:
- Option A — MongoDB Atlas: Cloud database. Create a cluster, database user, and configure network access. Copy the Node.js connection string from Atlas.
- Option B — Local MongoDB: If MongoDB Server is installed and running on your computer, use the local connection string.
MongoDB Atlas setup guide: Official MongoDB setup instructions. 
MongoDB Docs


Create a .env file:
PORT=3000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/day5_student_db


If you use Atlas, replace the MONGODB_URI value with your actual Atlas connection string. Don't upload .env or expose your database password on GitHub.

Create .gitignore:
node_modules/
.env
